			"heading": "Command Center at a glance",
			"text": "Select a numbered area to learn how it helps you read the dashboard and make informed decisions. 01 Application BarShow or hide the rail, choose the site, change theme, open help, or open Settings. The site picker sets which site the Pipeline and CalcEngines sections describe. Work Items and Site Scope do not depend on it. The picker stays unavailable until the first load finishes. A green dot pulsing beside the title means the background site sweep is running. It says nothing about the health of the site you are on. An amber dot beside a site name means that site's newest release has not finished publishing to every environment. Type * in the site search to see only those sites. See Sites with a release in flight below. The theme button cycles Dark, Light and System. The gear opens Settings, where Profile holds your sign-ins and Display holds your appearance preferences. 02 Navigation RailOne entry per section. A badge counts what in it needs you. Your saved work item queries sit under Work Items. Releases holds Pipeline and CalcEngines, Sentinel holds Site Scope, Site Metrics and RBLe Balancer, and Tools holds Grazer, Repository Status and the Diagnostics menu. A badge is amber when something waits on you and red when it needs more urgent attention. See Rail badges below for what each one counts. The footer names the selected site's repository. 03 Releases · PipelineThe release being compared and the one it is compared against, plus commit counts across repositories. The two chips read from → to. Hover either one to see who requested it, when it published, and the build it was cut from. The commit counts cover every repository the site is built from; click a repository to open the Pipeline page at its commits, or click the tile to open the page. 04 Releases · CalcEnginesThe CalcEngines associated with the selected site. The total comes first, then one chip per environment reading ENV: count: how many CalcEngines have their newest version in that environment. The chips add up to the total. Click a chip to open CalcEngines with that environment selected in Show; a zero-count chip opens All. Click a checkout row to filter by its email. The blocking count identifies upper (_PROD) checkouts that can block the TFS Release Pipeline. 05 RBLe Balancer KPIOne balancer's nodes: state, response time, load and share of traffic. The header gives the request rate and counts nodes by state. Each node's row shows its average response time, CPU and memory meters, its share of traffic over the last 10 seconds and its gate. The dots and arrows switch balancers; click the tile to open RBLe Balancer. See The KPI tile. 06 Site Scope KPIOne cell per monitored site, worst first. Hover any cell to see the site, its state, and who is on call for it. The counts leave out any state with nothing in it. The slowest sites and the sites with errors in the last hour are links that open Site Scope filtered to that site. 07 Site Metrics KPILogins, page requests, calculation requests, and errors. It is titled after the site you are on. Site Metrics shows representative sample values, dimmed behind a Coming Soon chip, until the real metrics source is finished. 08 What's HappeningOne list of what needs you and what is moving right now. Each row is a sentence naming the site and what happened. Click a row to go to its section, switching site first if the row is about another one. The coloured counts on the right total the rows by colour (red, amber, blue for in progress, green for finished, grey for information), and the header's \"need you\" count is the rows marked amber or red. See What's Happening below for the full rules."
