			"anchor": "sentinel-balancer",
			"title": "Settings",
			"heading": "Sentinel · Balancer",
			"text": "Setting Publishing Nodes Sentinel endpoints that hold the server credentials to replace an RBLe API's appsettings files. Each has a unique name and a unique http:// or https:// endpoint without a user name or password. Drag a node by its grip to reorder. Renaming a node keeps the balancers that use it; removing one clears their Use For Settings Publishing, and the footer says so before you save. Publishing nodes are not contacted on Save. RBLe Balancers One per environment, shown on the Dashboard tile and the RBLe Balancer page whichever site is selected. Add, edit, undo, remove and reorder them like Work Items queries; edits apply when you save. Save signs in to each new or edited balancer's Sentinel endpoint with your KAT Management credentials and reads it, and stops with the reason when the endpoint cannot be reached, denies you, has no balancer configured, or does not report the cluster. When every failure is one Sentinel could not confirm (it could not be reached, denied you, or failed some other way), Save anyway under the list saves without that check; the RBLe Balancer page then reports any problem. Name, Cluster, Deployment Type The name is how the balancer is shown everywhere, and must be unique. Cluster is the balancer cluster to watch (default Primary), matched to the cluster's key or display name and saved in Sentinel's spelling; each endpoint can watch a cluster once. Deployment Type (default Live) says which deployment's settings files Update Settings replaces. Sentinel Endpoint The Sentinel API for this environment, an absolute http:// or https:// URL without a user name or password. Balancers that share an endpoint share one read. Poll Every (seconds) How often the balancer is read while the Dashboard or the RBLe Balancer page is showing. 1 to 60; default 2. Use For Settings Publishing The publishing node, listed by name, that reads and replaces this balancer's appsettings files. With None, View Settings, Update Settings and Update All Settings are unavailable. Host Names In the editor's Hosts section. The web servers running the balancer in this environment, comma separated: at least one, at most 25, each a plain host name without dots. Each must be the web server's machine name. The RBLe Balancer page reads the first one until you choose another in its Host picker, and node actions go to every one of them. A web server that answers but is not listed is reported as an unknown host. Always replace existing files when downloading settings files Under View Settings Download. View Settings saves a node's file to your Downloads folder as {node}.{file name}. On, an existing file of that name is replaced without asking; off, you are asked whether to replace it, save it somewhere else, or cancel. Off by default. Automatically open settings files after download Opens the saved file in Visual Studio Code when it is installed, otherwise in the app Windows uses for the file. On by default. Show confirmation after downloading settings files Show the saved path with Copy Path, Open Folder and Open File after each download. On by default. Not used while settings files open automatically."
