			"anchor": "create-queries",
			"title": "Work Items",
			"heading": "Creating Queries Views",
			"text": "Follow the steps below to link TFS queries to KAT Command Center. Queries are added, edited and removed on the Work Items page of Settings. Visit TFS Work Items. Create a new query or select existing query under 'My Queries' (or select existing under 'KAT Queries') After selecting a query, the address will be something like .../_workitems?id=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001&_a=query. Copy the query ID (i.e. 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001). In KAT Command Center, open Settings with the Settings button in the app bar, choose Work Items, and click Add above the Queries list (shown above). Fill in the configuration shown below, then press the footer's Save to put the query in the list. Press Save again to save Settings. The new query appears under Work Items in the rail without a refresh. While the Add/Edit query pane is open, the footer's Cancel and Save act on this one query - the Query Edits label above them says so. To change a query later, press Edit on its row. No query edits, additions, or deletions are saved until you press Save from any of the main Settings pages, and Cancel discards all of it. See Settings for explanation of Work Query settings."
