			"title": "Work Items",
			"heading": "Work Item Detail",
			"text": "Work Item detail displays all task details, comment history and access to download attachments. If an item has a client KAT tag but is not itself tagged KAT Spec Sheet, matching spec sheet attachments are shown in a separate row. Notable Features 'Click to copy' ID and Title to easily share or use in commit comments and messages/emails The banner carries who has it and how it got there - Assigned To, Assigned By, Created By and when it last changed - then the classification it was filed under: Type / State, Priority / Severity, and its tags. The header's ⋯ menu holds Edit Task, Triage, Return Task and Close Task, then View in TFS, Copy Link and Copy ID. The row's ⋯ menu has the same actions. Attachment chips enable file download. If a task tag matches a spec sheet attachment, it will be displayed in a separate row for easy access. Keyboard warriors rejoice. Keyboard Shortcuts provide quick access to all the actions you need to manage a work item efficiently. Comments show newest first with who wrote them and when (hover a time for the exact date). Click a person's avatar to show only their comments; click them again to show everyone. Newest/Oldest flips the order. A long description or repro steps is trimmed with a Show full link, such as Show full repro steps. People show as coloured initials, replaced by their TFS profile photo a moment after the modal opens if they have one. The photos load in the background, so they never hold the comments up, and anyone without a photo simply keeps their initials. Related Work, Commits and Builds tabs show linked work items, associated commits and integrated builds; each tab shows its count. History shows how the item got where it is. Two lanes along the top trace its State and Owner, one stop per change with how long each lasted; a long lane collapses to +N, which expands it (Show less folds it back). Below, every save is listed newest first by day, with each field's old and new value and any link added or removed. One person's back-to-back saves show as one entry, led by \"N saves\"; the window is set in Settings > Work Items > History. A save that added a comment has a comment button that opens that comment on the Details tab. Links TFS added on its own, such as a build that integrated the item, are marked automatic."
