			"text": "The Return Triaged button puts the grid into select mode. It disables itself and adds a row below the filters with Return Tasks:, an All box, how many are ticked, Continue and Cancel. A checkbox appears before every applicable ID, but only the rows already at Triaged offer one: the work you just finished, which goes back to whoever handed it over. Continue opens the dialog below. Dismissing it keeps the ticks so you can change them. Cancel or Esc leaves select mode. Keyboard warriors, see Keyboard Shortcuts for details on how ticking and navigation can be done from the keyboard. Notable Features Every field is prefilled: Return To with whoever owned the item before you, Triage with Pending, and the comment with your Default Return Task Comment. Change or clear what doesn't apply. Only the comment is optional. An item without a Return To blocks the submit and is marked in place. Pressing OK closes the dialog, and the row reads Processing… until every item is written; a Return cannot be cancelled once it starts, so its Cancel is hidden. Items that failed, or that changed since you ticked them (those are refreshed, not saved), are marked in the grid and listed with their reason above it. Select mode then ends. Retry on that list reopens the dialog with only those items, filled in with what you submitted. The list, and the chance to retry, are cleared by its ×, by pressing Return Triaged again, by submitting another Return, or by switching queries. Every item is written concurrently as one comment-plus-reassign-plus-Triage change, so the assigner sees a single revision rather than three."
