			"text": "Besides F5 (see above), the Tools > Repository Status table, its menus and its dialogs work from the keyboard. Checkout rows have a … actions button; branch rows do not have a menu. j / k Move down or up one row, wrapping at either end, through every row on screen, including an expanded repository's branch and worktree rows. A repository opened from What's Happening is already selected, so j/k continue from it. Space Opens the selected row's … menu. Branch rows have no menu, so it does nothing there. In batch mode it ticks the selected row instead. → / ← On a focused repository row, → expands it to show its branches and worktrees and ← collapses it. Expansion and focus survive background checks. Esc Closes an open menu first; otherwise unselects the row. Changing Show also unselects it. Enter / Space on … or ▾ Opens a row's actions menu or the Batch Action menu. A row menu first focuses its container. In a menu, ↑/↓ and Home/End move, → opens a remote's Fetch / Push / Force Push entries and ← closes them, Enter chooses, and Esc closes the menu and returns focus to its button. Pressing the button again also closes it. Space on a row checkbox In batch mode, ticks or clears that row; All in the header does every applicable row on screen. Continue runs the batch action, Cancel leaves batch mode, and so does Esc while you are still choosing rows; once the action is running, Cancel stops it instead. Esc in a dialog Cancels a Pull, Push, Commit or worktree delete review or another confirmation, changes nothing (a \"Don't ask me\" switch is saved only when you confirm), and returns focus to the control that opened it. Ctrl+Enter in the commit message Confirms the Commit review, like its button. Enter alone starts a new line."
